# slow loris Attack 
A Slowloris attack is a type of denial-of-service (DoS) attack that targets web servers by opening numerous connections to the server and keeping them open for as long as possible. The attack works by sending partial HTTP requests to the server, and then it continues to send subsequent headers at regular intervals to keep these connections alive. As a result, the server is unable to close the connections or accept new ones, eventually exhausting its resources and rendering the service unavailable to legitimate users.



